usiness. The company offers its services under the PHH Mortgage and Liberty Reverse Mortgage brands. It serves financial institutions. The company was formerly known as Ocwen Financial Corporation and changed its name to Onity Group Inc. in June 2024. Onity Group Inc. was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in West Palm Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Glen A. Messina | CEO, President & Chair of the Board | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $274K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Onity Group Inc. is a micro-cap financial services business with a $232M market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and -5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 96% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 86-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $751M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 51% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5050071530758227},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Ocwen Financial Corporation (ONIT) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/98/How_Ocwen_Financial_Corporation_ONIT_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_112526073001_1795609801.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795609801.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Onity Group (NYSE:ONIT) versus KindlyMD (NASDA